<title>AUSTRALIA: TABLE-Queensland 1997/98 budget revenue/outlays.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Queensland 1997/98 budget revenue/outlays.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian state of Queensland released its 1997/98 (July/June) budget on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The following is an excerpt from budget table 1.1 outlining aggregate revenues and expenditure for 1997/98.</p>
<p>		  CONSOLIDATED FUND BUDGET AGGREGATES (A$ MILLION)</p>
<p>				  Estimated	  Budget	Percent</p>
<p>				Actual  96/97	 97/98	change</p>
<p>Opening surplus		    5.4	     10.9</p>
<p>Receipts</p>
<p>-Commonwealth Payments	 5,231.7	5,189.6	  -0.8</p>
<p>-Taxes, fees, fines	    4,393.8	4,563.0	  +3.9</p>
<p>-Other state sources	   4,233.2	4,496.5	  +6.2</p>
<p>TOTAL RECEIPTS		  13,858.7     14,249.1	  +2.8</p>
<p>Outlays</p>
<p>-Recurrent Services	    7,950.7	8,237.3	  +3.6</p>
<p>-Debt Servicing		    289.0	  247.0	 -14.5</p>
<p>-Grants and subsidies	  2,236.1	2,306.5	  +3.1</p>
<p>-Capital			   1,832.5	2,275.6	 +24.2</p>
<p>-Financing Transactions	1,544.8	1,180.0	 -23.6</p>
<p>TOTAL OUTLAYS		   13,853.1     14,246.4	  +2.8</p>
<p>Closing surplus		     10.9	   13.6</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
